Started the `[server]` layer with its client registry. Clients are registry-backed records, exportable through GenericSetup like providers are, but their secrets are stored hashed with scrypt rather than masked: this package is the server here, so nothing ever needs the plaintext again. A secret is returned once when it is minted or rotated and cannot be read back. Redirect URIs match exactly, public clients are flagged as requiring PKCE, and an unknown client id costs the same work as a wrong secret so the two cannot be told apart. Installed by the new `server` GenericSetup profile, which is also what registers the browser layer everything else in the layer will bind to. @ericof
